  "notes_for_editor": "Structure of the history rests on LighthouseFriends and D'Entremont (secondary, copyrighted; paraphrased) because the NRHP nomination is an undigitised placeholder and the corpus holds no Light-House Board volumes before 1891 with a station entry. The 1838 Carpender and 1842 Lewis reports and the 1888 red cut are quoted second-hand and named as such. Tower dates disagree: wooden tower Oct 1784 (LF), Dec 1784 (marker), 1785 (NEL); stone tower Oct 1817 (marker) vs 1818 (LF, NEL). Rebuild cost: $2M appropriated vs just over $1M spent. Owner conflict: record says Trustees, Trustees page says federally owned lighthouse. Roster conflict: USLHS has Willis Higgins 1897-1903; D'Entremont has Nickerson 1897-1903. Bulletin items are matched in OCR with columns interleaved (1917 p.16: the A. T. Serrell item). Bulletin pages are PDF pages. 'NRHP 1982 listing' not stated in story (only Wikipedia). Boston Light link (Haskins) is us-ma-boston, verify. Newspaper 1904 ice item skipped (OCR fragmentary). Checker: dedication date conflict (marker heading 6 Sep 1986 vs 7 Sep in sources 2,3) now stated in text. NEL says the last keeper's son was Bill Grieder (Frank Grieder 1935-37 in USLHS), at odds with LighthouseFriends calling Haskins the last principal keeper; text attributes the claim. Bulletin 1917 p.16 Serrell item verified on the page image (printed p.264).",
